editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:19:| 57 | Not At His Desk | 4,959 | All cutaway. **The morning clerk** (895): the protected first sentence; four keys in a row; the swept cupboard; the ash; the summaries, still pinned eleven years later. The personnel query (MARKER) and **the apparatus** (1,020): *What did he have?*; fifteen years of product called up, true and empty; nobody knows what he kept. **Seln's window** (3,050): nineteen bundles into the stove; the keys; the orchard; the case's history; looking back from a crest, badly, at one lamp; the eighteenth stone; forty of Karis's paces; firewood; the last return written and used to light the fire. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:| 59 | The Registry Line | 7,690 | What the road still had; hay paid once; Brom shoes the watcher's cob; the long climb. The last chartered waystation: "You've boxes."; the board (MARKER); the station's stamp in a drawer; the tier notice with a hay sum. The Fourth-day; the provincial pillar; the last watcher's nod to Brom. The walkable ford and the old toll board. The last station: swept, the roof on carter's wire, the book that stops four years ago on an open line, the sigil in older stone. Five crossings of the sill. Cael at the frame-house door (MARKER). The turning place; "Nobody's watching."; the only clock east of here. Rain; the first night outside any jurisdiction; the reply to Daeva (MARKER). The post-rider at the ford; "Both promises ride east with me." The first ridge, the horse blowing, three boxes by hand; the entry. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:30:| 1 | ch55 : 187 | `Gault's last note, ending *The instruments will not see its like.*` | A small leaf from Gault's book in the panel-note hand, left at the counter before the first bell, dated for the day, to be entered with the withdrawal; Bracken turns it round for Cael to read. After the marker Cael re-reads the last line, which is quoted once (*The instruments will not see its like.*). If the unit already ends on that line, the repeat is deliberate; cut it if it reads double. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:31:| 2 | ch57 : 47 | `the personnel query` | Bracken's query to the district office that placed the teaching assistant, in the First-day bag. The next line says "It was a single leaf, and it asked where a man was." If the protected query is the registry's own instrument and not the house's, the two sentences before the marker want one clause changed. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:35:| 6 | ch60 : 345 | `the closing exchange, first line (Cael: "I have nine things that aren't a Path…")` | Said aloud by Cael at the fire, to all four, straight after Seln forecasts the file's new line. The three following lines are verbatim from §8 with my attribution: Lira "Let them escalate. They'll need better maps."; Brom "And better roads."; Cael "Noted." |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:37:Units that §8 gives **whole** and that I used verbatim, as instructed, although the task lists them as "to check": **"Nobody's watching."** (ch59, Brom) and the log entry ***First look at the edge territories. Everyone warns you the world out here isn't governed. Nobody mentions that it's big.*** (ch59's last line; the entry is exactly those three sentences and nothing is added to it). If either is longer in the protected source, it drops in whole.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:41:**Calendar.** No season or month names; feet, yards and paces; Halcenvane weekdays; **no day numbers on the page** beyond the book's own "eighth day" and "fourth day of the year". By the binding count: **Day 203, Seventh-day:** the counter after the first bell; Gault's note; the assistant; the room; Lira's seminar at the third bell; the wing; Brom's boxes; the district officer; three trips; the gate; the bluff road at dusk; the ferry; the guesting-house in Ostrand. **Night of 203:** Seln leaves by the farm track and Ostrand bridge. **Day 204, First-day:** not at his desk; Bracken's query; the four leave Ostrand at first light; first ford; one watcher; the eighteenth stone at dusk — five. **Day 205:** the second ford; a waystation. **Day 206:** the long climb; the last chartered waystation. **Day 207, Fourth-day:** the year closes; the frame-house is opened for nobody; the provincial pillar at noon and the watcher's last line; the walkable ford; the last station, where they sleep. **Day 208, Fifth-day:** five crossings; **the Line crossed in the morning — after day 207**; "Nobody's watching."; rain; the first night outside any jurisdiction (no fire); the reply written. **Day 209, Sixth-day — the second day past the Line:** the ford in spate and the westbound post-rider; the first ridge; the scree; the shelf; the first fire; the inventory. **The book ends on the evening of day 209.** The machine's week and Vastin's window run in office time from day 203 to some days past the close.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:80:- **Brom:** "I know what it was for."; the envelope set down; five boxes and not one his; "No."; "Three boxes."; "I check."; the cob's shoe; "I'm Copper on that side of this stone"; "Nobody's watching."; the sixth cup; the load rule.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:85:- **Rooke:** "Higher. Till it stops beating."; "Doors open both ways."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:95:- **The new line:** *Status: active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.* — entered by a faceless clerk from a slip of advice with no office's mark; "Nobody had signed for the line. No office was named on it." The file is not tied; it goes on a shelf "where it could be reached".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:102:- **Closed:** the clean door; the four withdrawals; Karis's standing; Lira's sentence to Rooke and the red book's words; Brom's two boxes; the watchers; the reply to Daeva; the first pole's fate (kept, and joined by the second).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121:- **Cael:** eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted Tide-adjacent anomaly** (*Still open. Still real. Patience.*). **Deployment since the Line: none.** The forearm bruise is a week old and about a week from gone; no open injury. Shadow sealed on Seln's terms; it costs from waking and drifts at dusk; its term is nearly met out here and he has left it shut. Hesk's book has about a third of its leaves.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:125:- **Behind them:** the file reads *Enrollment: closed by resignation. Proceedings: moot. Re-evaluation: not executed. Asset-restriction: pending jurisdiction. Status: active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.* The last watcher turned back at the provincial pillar on day 207. The faction is unnamed, unfaced and unlocated, and made no third move. Vastin is inside, an instrument no longer, and returned the summary unannotated. Withrow, Bracken, Rooke, Gault and Ephram are at Halcenvane; the assistant keeps the lamp lit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:141:- **The machine's week (flag; texts mine round the protected status words):** the seat's clerk's *Moot.*; the frame-house hour; the junior chair's line; the five answers; the clerk's "served within the hour". **A second visit to Denvash in the recess** (one clause, so that the caliper visit is the third). **Hesk:** "a great many shavings"; brass a third dearer; a receipt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:160:Verbatim, grep-checked: "Your files are in order. All four." (ch56, split by the attribution) · "Doors open both ways." (ch56, Rooke to Brom) · "Seln simply wasn't at his desk the next morning." (ch57, first sentence) · *pending jurisdiction* (ch58 ×3) · "Nobody's watching." (ch59) · *First look at the edge territories…* (ch59) · *Still open. Still real. Patience.* (ch60) · *Reydan will get his answer…Good.* (ch60) · the first pole whole, re-read (ch60) · *I can work within the system. The system was never designed to include me.* (ch60) · *active non-compliance, observation priority escalated* (ch60, bible form) · "Let them escalate. They'll need better maps." / "And better roads." / "Noted." (ch60) · "the hand with no face" (ch60 inventory) · Seln's catechism, second line (ch57).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:164:**Composed, and flagged:** the inventory (the packet lists it as protected; §8 gives no text beyond "the hand with no face" and the three words — owner flag 3); Bracken's off-procedure speech round "I was wrong" and "I intend to keep true records anyway" (§3 quotes it with an ellipsis; it is not a §8 unit).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169:- **Overlap:** `ed.sh overlap book-06-the-compacts-hand 9` first listed **4 unprotected runs**. Three were chance: "she did not sit and she did not" (ch58); and two phrases I had taken from the Book 7 map's summary of the seam, which turn out to be the source's own words — "and it was more than any of them had expected" and "had about a third of its leaves left" (ch60). All three were re-composed. The fourth is the packet's own line. **Final: 1 unprotected, 12 protected.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:170:- **Proposed protected pattern (not applied; `protected-patterns.txt` untouched):**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:176:- The probe was run without `SHOW`, so I have chapter figures only. The skeleton hits in ch58 and ch60 will sit on the status words and the protected log lines.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:208:1. **Six protected units are marked, not written** (table above). The chapters cannot be rendered to audio until they are supplied. Two of them carry a guess about form that the coordinator should check when dropping the text in: the reply to Daeva is called "short" in the next sentence, and the personnel query is framed as the house's question to the district office.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:210:3. **The inventory is my composition.** The packet lists "the inventory" as protected, but §8 gives no text for it. I wrote it in the edition's own form (ch34's birthday inventory), with nine lines, a blank the width of a name in the Anchor line, "the hand with no face", and the three words. If the source's inventory must stand, it replaces ch60 lines from *What I carry: nine confirmed.* to *Under all nine, the still place I don't count.*; the paragraphs after it refer only to "nine lines", "the gap" and "the stair".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:211:4. **Attributions I chose without the source:** "Nobody's watching." is **Brom's** (Seln asks that somebody else say it). In the closing exchange, **Lira** says "Let them escalate. They'll need better maps." and **Brom** "And better roads." "Both promises ride east with me." is **spoken by Cael to Lira**. "They can only decline to count it" is **Bracken's**. "You've boxes." is the keeper's first words. Each can be re-hung without touching the scene.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:213:6. **The last line.** The Book 7 map quotes Book 6's last line as "nothing anywhere was deciding what he was, except him." It is not in §8 or the packet, so I did not copy it; mine reads "There was nothing left anywhere that was deciding what he was. There was only him." If the owner wants the source's sentence, it is a one-line swap and a new protected pattern.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:224:17. **Proposed protected pattern:** one (the class line, above). `protected-patterns.txt` untouched.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.md:5:**CLOSE WITH FIXES.** All six marker units exist in the source and must be restored. The closing inventory also has protected source wording; the packet's protection is not cancelled by its omission from `BOOK_MAP.md` §8. The source last line is binding through the Book 7 seam and must replace the author's paraphrase. Three attribution rulings require repair: Lira, not Brom, first says “Nobody's watching”; “Both promises ride east with me” is a log entry, not speech to Lira; and Karis, not Cael, says/writes “Noted.” Lira's and Brom's two lines in the closing exchange are correct.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.md:13:Standing-ruling audit: the fixes introduce no season, month or English weekday name and no metric unit; Movement 9 already uses feet and yards. Instrument prose already uses *Caelen Hesk-ward* (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:71`, `manuscript/chapter-58.md:69`). Mandatory departures from source wording are confined to the personnel-query role/calendar/house frame, `Since my Kindling`, `Nine fragments`, and `two renewals on paper`; each is identified below. The ratified day-203/day-207/Line order is preserved.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.md:19:Governing text: `BOOK_MAP.md:618` protects “Gault's last note, ending *The instruments will not see its like.*” The complete source unit is:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.md:21:> *Assay-provision enrollment: resigned in good standing prior to revocation date. Baseline file: closed complete. Four terms of evaluation-linked observation, no adverse finding, no anomaly of conduct. The evaluator of record notes that the file closes on the enrollee's own act and not the registry's, and that this is the correct closing, and the only just one available. The instruments will not see its like.* (`books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-21.md:59`)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.md:52:No standing-ruling change is needed inside the protected reply. The following sentence does need the separately listed join fix: the restored reply is not usefully described there as “short.”
