editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/review-cold.stdout.log:3259:*Status: active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/review-cold.stdout.log:3287:"I have nine things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no enrollment, no protection — and four people who signed out of the world that was supposed to provide them, and one of the nine taken from a hand the world sent to hold me, and one taken in earnest from a friend, and the machine's own maintenance records in a case under that canvas, which we can't file and can't publish and are carrying east anyway because the truth is worth carrying even when it can't be spent."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/review-cold.stdout.log:3349:+I expect the next event to be contact with the first eastern hold, where the five will have to trade, navigate, and test capabilities without registry categories or reliable maps. I also expect the “active non-compliance” machinery to seek a new way to observe them, and the unnamed Anchor-adjacent source to become a live problem rather than a blank in an inventory.
