editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/source-tracking.stdout.log:1198:    63	For the first time since a first posting nineteen years and a life ago, there was no desk to file it at, no chain to file it up, no cover it protected, no self it maintained. There was a road, and a case, and a man walking east toward the first honest employment of his adult life. He let the report dissolve where it stood. The dissolving felt like nothing he had a word for, and he did not reach for the word, because reaching for words about himself was a habit he had never had and was too old to acquire.
