editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:2289:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:1427:| 22 | Both Roads | 4,790 | 5 | Brom tips the chair: **"Prepare both roads." "Win the sittings. Keep a box."** — Lira counts three. The word *box* stays. Shirts, all the strapping, the plaque ("If I leave it, you'll go back for it"); hand to the LEFT pocket; **"It's the second box that's the problem."** — the sealed letter, twenty-three days; nobody asks. **Cael's first pole at full strength**, from the bottom: Pellin as a woman with a brass plate, eleven seconds, fourteen; forward through Vell, Greyvane, the grant and two renewals on paper, the inspection, Norhold's clause, Umber's *no number goes here*; "People change with the weather. Text doesn't." **"I'm not leaving the room while the text still works."** He pre-empts the objection; "always Karis who read it." **Karis names it an induction** (a run; "Every rule anybody ever broke looked exactly like this the evening before"; a tally, not a guarantee). **Lira: Fenmark's perfect form; "It's not ground. It's a floor."**; joists somebody laid; *Both roads* — it costs Cael nothing and nobody makes him pay. Seln's two looks. The slow spirit kettle; Karis: "Memory improves things"; **"It was the night we asked."** Seln lights them up the dairy step and crosses to the wing. Log. **SELN cutaway (~2,330), the dark wing**: no lamp, the fire-watch's square on the counter; his one correction examined (forty days as a narrow door); fifteen years, nineteen postings, sixty-three subjects, the followed few; the maintenance records copied twelve years ago on his fourth posting, understood in a green corridor between two appointments — *whose question it had been*; the boy inferred (the mill-town table; two slips burned on the coals; a season that never settled; Norhold spent on purpose); his own true, empty reports filed with the boy's receipts; the brass key held and returned; the dairy step and the lamp he held for each of them; ***The deciding has stopped being quiet.*** |
