editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:4346:editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:1078:- `ed.sh overlap book-02-iron-circuit 2`: **0 unprotected, 4 protected** (unchanged).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:4418:editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:4722:books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:406:The ledger of the year, in its established forms. The Power Log inventory, in Hesk's satchel, by an inn's fire, shown complete: **ten confirmed fragments** — Wind-adjacent (Lira), Pressure-adjacent (Feryn), Iron-adjacent (Brom), Compression-adjacent (Reydan), Ember-adjacent (Karis), Shadow-adjacent (Seln), Storm-adjacent (Daeva), Anchor-adjacent (unnamed), Blade-adjacent (Ephram), Tide-adjacent (Oryn) — ten integrated abilities, deployment notes current, the tenth carrying the field none of the others carry, *clinical*; and the anomaly, session nine, no longer an anomaly *entry* but a *location*: "The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues." One log line for the old promises: "Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map." Letters, on the last ferry: Hesk's package, at last, six weeks late — instrument-maker's work, a *straightedge*, brass, folding, calibrated in a hand Cael knows, and the note in full: *"Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H."* Cael looks at Karis's map, and at the straightedge, and does not say anything, and the chapter does not need him to. To Hesk, west: *"Nineteen, past the Line, and there's a roof. It's an inn. The shape you said to mind is a line, and I've got the tool for it now. — C."* To Vell, because her ledger holds his first honest record and Pike's holds his newest, and she will want to know there is a second ledger-keeper on the continent who stopped numbering him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:4426:editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:4799:books/book-04-copper-crown/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:268:*Close on:* the inventory, updated in the new pen's first use: six confirmed fragments. One anomaly — session nine, Tide-adjacent, turned over once, same three words: *Still open. Still real. Patience.* And a last line for the year's second half: "Sixteen. Six fragments. The Compact's best watcher watching out for me instead, and no way to thank him for it that wouldn't burn him. Semester evaluation in nine weeks. Whatever the system sends to watch it — we're ready. We built ready."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:4443:editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:4909:books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:365:The last chapter — the ledger, the file, and the door into Arc 3, in the series' Chapter 24 register: small leavings and stayings, each heavier than its size. The first true edge-territories camp: a switchback shelf above an unnamed valley, firelight, the found family's roles running on new terrain with old grammar — Brom's quiet competence now aimed at load-balancing a cart instead of acquiring dinner twice over; Karis indexing her three boxes into a working field-archive; Lira mapping tomorrow's route like a bracket sheet; Seln gone for an hour and back with the lay of every approach, unasked; Ephram's absence at the fire noted once, without grief — he stayed, and staying was right for him, and the family's arithmetic holds him anyway. The ledger of the year, in its established forms. The Power Log inventory, in Hesk's satchel, by firelight, shown complete: **nine confirmed fragments** — Wind-adjacent (Lira), Pressure-adjacent (Feryn), Iron-adjacent (Brom), Compression-adjacent (Reydan), Ember-adjacent (Karis), Shadow-adjacent (Seln), Storm-adjacent (Daeva), Anchor-adjacent (unnamed), Blade-adjacent (Ephram) — nine integrated abilities, each with a name beside it except the one the system sent namelessly, and the anomaly, session nine, Tide-adjacent, turned over once, closed with the standing three words: *Still open. Still real. Patience.* One log line for the old promises: "Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. The road east is long. Good." Letters, held for the next westbound courier whenever one exists: to Hesk (*"Eighteen, unenrolled, and past the Line. The shape you said to mind — I minded it. The tools fit the road. — C."*), to Vell, because her ledger holds his first honest record and the resignation belongs in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:4467:editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5119:books/book-03-no-path-given/chapters/chapter-15.md:83:"I'm going to tell you the shape of the next three weeks," she said, "so that nobody wastes any of them pretending. The academy's counsel will fight the procedure — timing, scope, document schedules. That buys days, not outcomes. The provision's language is what has protected you, and the provision's language is exactly what he's chosen to attack, which means the man has read our file as carefully as we've kept it." A breath. "I staked my professional standing on the argument that you'd be established fact before anyone looked closely. You are established fact. Two months of clean assessments, a public exhibition, panel records. He looked closely anyway, and he's betting that fact loses to category." She looked at him, and there was something underneath the flatness he had never quite seen in her before — not fear; closer to a debt being acknowledged. "I recruited you into this exposure, Cael. Whatever the next three weeks ask of me, they can have."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:4481:editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5268:He filled nine pages of the notebook with nothing but the code's history of flinching. Every defensive amendment was a scar, and a scar was a record of a wound, and a wound meant that at some point, somewhere, somebody had found a gap in the text and driven something through it hard enough to make the Compact bleed. He catalogued the scars the way he'd catalogue an opponent's guard: not because any single one of them was his opening, but because the pattern of where a system protected itself told you where it had learned to be afraid — and, more usefully, where it had never learned to be.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:4565:editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:6534:He had the evidence, if she'd demanded it, because he'd been assembling it for weeks without admitting to himself what it was for. Her last six wins, watched from the crowd's edge with the same attention he gave anyone: in every one, she'd had a faster, riskier line available and had declined it. He'd timed her decision points against his breath-count, and the pattern held across all six — at each branching moment, she took the option that protected the win over the option that tested the technique. Against Iron-equivalent opponents, that choice was always available to her, because her reads were good enough to see both branches. That was precisely what made it holding back. A fighter who couldn't see the risky line wasn't declining anything. She saw it every time, and every time she paid for certainty with information, and the ledger recorded the certainty and nobody recorded the price.
