editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6398:   143	Rooke's goodbye to Brom was four words, delivered at the gate with the coaching file nowhere in sight: "Doors open both ways."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6421:     3	Seln simply wasn't at his desk the next morning.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6481:    63	For the first time since a first posting nineteen years and a life ago, there was no desk to file it at, no chain to file it up, no cover it protected, no self it maintained. There was a road, and a case, and a man walking east toward the first honest employment of his adult life. He let the report dissolve where it stood. The dissolving felt like nothing he had a word for, and he did not reach for the word, because reaching for words about himself was a habit he had never had and was too old to acquire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6678:   113	"Nobody's watching."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6682:   117	"Nobody's watching," Cael agreed, and charted the absence the way he had charted the presence for four years, and found the chart had no entries in it, and left the page blank, because a blank page was the honest record of the thing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6712:   147	*The rematch stands. Not postponed — relocated. It happens on a floor nobody owns, and I think you'd prefer that anyway; a Gold-tier fact and an unclassified one, fighting where no seal can score either of us, is the only honest version of the bout, and we both knew it at Norhold. Find me when you're ready to fight something no ladder built. I'll be east.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6742:   177	*First look at the edge territories. Everyone warns you the world out here isn't governed. Nobody mentions that it's big.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6789:    47	*Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — Feryn. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — source protected, sealed still, the logic updated and the discipline held: a defector's tradecraft in my hands would confirm the surveillance-era acquisition, so the seal stays, and Seln knows now that it does, and knows why, which changes nothing about the seal and everything about the debt. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; the piece of the machine itself. Blade-adjacent — Ephram; the only "non-hostile" in the log; taken in earnest from a friend who asked to be shown straight.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6791:    49	*Nine integrated abilities. Each with a name beside it, one of them protected and one of them missing — and the missing line I have left blank on purpose, because the blank is the truest thing the entry says.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6793:    51	*One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Turned over once, per the custom at intervals that matter — checked against the cache, checked against everything the cache explained, and touching none of it. Still open. Still real. Patience.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6809:    67	*Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. The road east is long, and it runs the right direction. Good.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6829:    87	He wrote that last sentence three times before he kept it, because the first two versions were warnings dressed as news and the man deserved news dressed as news, and because Hesk had spent a lifetime declining to be protected by people who loved him and would decline it again by return of post, in about eleven words, and would be right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:6873:   131	"I have nine things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no enrollment, no protection — and four people who signed out of the world that was supposed to provide them, and one of the nine taken from a hand the world sent to hold me, and one taken in earnest from a friend, and the machine's own maintenance records in a case under that canvas, which we can't file and can't publish and are carrying east anyway because the truth is worth carrying even when it can't be spent."
