editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11201:+- **“Nobody's watching.” — wrong.** Lira says it first in the source; Cael then agrees (`books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-23.md:111-117`). The manuscript gives it to Brom at `manuscript/chapter-59.md:323`.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11243:+   [[TIER-B: Gault's last note, ending *The instruments will not see its like.* — coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11249:+   *Assay-provision enrollment: resigned in good standing prior to revocation date. Baseline file: closed complete. Four terms of evaluation-linked observation, no adverse finding, no anomaly of conduct. The evaluator of record notes that the file closes on the enrollee's own act and not the registry's, and that this is the correct closing, and the only just one available. The instruments will not see its like.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11257:+   [[TIER-B: the personnel query — coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11271:+   [[TIER-B: the waystation board — coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11285:+   [[TIER-B: "You couldn't read me… Thanks for the eleven seconds." — coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11299:+   [[TIER-B: Cael's reply to Daeva (Tier A: *The rematch stands. Not postponed — relocated. It happens on a floor nobody owns…*, whole) — coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11307:+   *The rematch stands. Not postponed — relocated. It happens on a floor nobody owns, and I think you'd prefer that anyway; a Gold-tier fact and an unclassified one, fighting where no seal can score either of us, is the only honest version of the bout, and we both knew it at Norhold. Find me when you're ready to fight something no ladder built. I'll be east.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11331:+   [[TIER-B: the closing exchange, first line (Cael: "I have nine things that aren't a Path…") — coordinator to supply protected text]]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11337:+   "I have nine things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no enrollment, no protection — and four people who signed out of the world that was supposed to provide them, and one of the nine taken from a hand the world sent to hold me, and one taken in earnest from a friend, and the machine's own maintenance records in a case under that canvas, which we can't file and can't publish and are carrying east anyway because the truth is worth carrying even when it can't be spent."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11365:+   *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — Feryn. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — source protected, sealed still, the logic updated and the discipline held: a defector's tradecraft in my hands would confirm the surveillance-era acquisition, so the seal stays, and Seln knows now that it does, and knows why, which changes nothing about the seal and everything about the debt. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; the piece of the machine itself. Blade-adjacent — Ephram; the only "non-hostile" in the log; taken in earnest from a friend who asked to be shown straight.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11367:+   *Nine fragments. Each with a name beside it, one of them protected and one of them missing — and the missing line I have left blank on purpose, because the blank is the truest thing the entry says.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11369:+   *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Turned over once, per the custom at intervals that matter — checked against the cache, checked against everything the cache explained, and touching none of it. Still open. Still real. Patience.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11393:+   *Still open. Still real. Patience.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-009/protected-text.stdout.log:11407:+   *I can work within the system. I have the receipts: a hearing, a provision, a stamp renewed four times, a tournament their own clause put me in. The system has text, and text has held me every time the people failed. This is more text. We'll read it better than they do. We always have.*
